## **English Contemplation**

Consciousness does not become the eye, mind or intellect; it lends them the light by which their functions are known.

An object may exist in the empirical world, but it becomes part of our lived experience through the senses, mind and intellect. Bondage does not begin merely because something is perceived. It begins when perception is joined by ownership, expectation and self-identification.

The seen does not command us to become attached. The mind projects fulfilment upon it, and the ego declares, “This is mine; without this I am incomplete.”

Witnessing is therefore not withdrawal from life. It is the freedom to see sensation, desire and reaction before they harden into compulsion. From this inner clarity, ethical action becomes possible.

The Self illumines attachment and freedom alike, yet remains untouched by both.

---

## **मुख्य सूत्र**

> **बुद्धि, मन और इन्द्रियाँ स्वयंप्रकाश नहीं; आत्मचैतन्य से प्रकाशित हैं।**

> **दृश्य का ज्ञान बन्धन नहीं; उसके साथ जुड़ा “मैं–मेरा” बन्धन है।**

> **चैतन्य प्रकाशित करता है; अहंकार स्वामित्व ग्रहण करता है।**

> **आसक्ति वस्तु में नहीं—वस्तु पर आरोपित सुख और पूर्णता की माँग में है।**

> **अनासक्ति त्यागी हुई वस्तु नहीं; त्यागा हुआ मिथ्या आश्रय है।**

> **साक्षीभाव निष्क्रियता नहीं—प्रतिक्रिया से मुक्त धर्मपूर्ण कर्म है।**

